# Accepted risks for the Terraform scan. Each entry needs a reason and is reviewed in the pull request.

# State bucket (terraform/bootstrap) uses S3-managed encryption (AES256), not a customer-managed KMS key.
# Accepted for the lab: the bucket is private, versioned and holds only Terraform state.
AWS-0132
AVD-AWS-0132

# Load balancer is internet-facing by design: it is the only public entry point,
# protected by AWS WAF, and forwards only to the API tasks on port 8000.
AWS-0053
AVD-AWS-0053

# KNOWN GAP: HTTP listener only. HTTPS needs a domain and an ACM certificate (optional Day 22).
# Remove these two lines when HTTPS is added.
AWS-0054
AVD-AWS-0054

# CloudTrail logs use S3-managed encryption (AES256), not a customer-managed KMS key.
# Accepted for the lab: private audit bucket, HTTPS-only bucket policy, log file validation on.
# Next step: dedicated KMS key with a CloudTrail key policy.
AWS-0015
AVD-AWS-0015
